]$ \n-  $[12, 18, 4, 7, 5]$ \n-  $[18, 4, 7, 5, 9]$ \n-  $[12, 18, 4, 7, 5, 9]$ \nTherefore, $f(a) = 12$. It can be proven that no other arrangement yields a smaller value of $f(a)$.	[{"input": "5\\n6\\n12 7 9 4 18 5\\n4\\n3 6 2 8\\n7\\n1 10 15 20 3 6 9\\n5\\n11 14 21 2 5\\n3\\n6 6 6", "output": "12 18 4 7 5 9\\n2 8 3 6\\n6 10 20 1 15 3 9\\n21 5 11 2 14\\n6 6 6"}]	2026-10-29 16:43:30.457	2026-10-29 15:49:10.551	2026-10-29 16:43:30.458	256	2000
