ect. In the second month, $11$ projects are distributed among $4$ employees: each gets $2$ projects, and Monocarp completes $3$ projects. The answer is $1 + 3 = 4$.\n\nIn the third test case, the number of projects completed by Monocarp in the six months is $2$, $1$, $0$, $5$, $5$, and $5$, respectively. Their sum is $2 + 1 + 0 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 18$.	[{"input": "7\\n1 1 1\\n3 10 2\\n3 8 6\\n7 20 1\\n10 25 100\\n8 36 17\\n1 999900 1000000000000", "output": "0\\n4\\n18\\n6\\n1425\\n110\\n999898177699820694"}]	2026-10-29 16:36:49.306	2026-10-29 15:49:10.551	2026-10-29 16:36:49.307	512	2000
