r target.\n\nIn the second test case, regardless of rearranging $a$, Alice can always find the sequence $[1,2,3]$ as her target sequence.\n\nIn the third test case,there is no rearrangement of $a$ that can prevent Alice from achieving her target. For example, for $a=[0,2,1]$, Alice can find the sequence $[1,2,3,2,3]$ as her target sequence.	[{"input": "6\\n3 2\\n0 1 2\\n3 3\\n0 1 2\\n3 6\\n0 1 2\\n3 4\\n0 1 2\\n3 10\\n0 1 2\\n5 1000\\n2 0 1 1 2", "output": "0 1 2\\n-1\\n-1\\n0 2 1 \\n-1\\n-1"}]	2026-10-29 16:39:38.591	2026-10-29 15:49:10.605	2026-10-29 16:39:38.592	256	1000
